How did Deep Learning evolve toward modern NLP?

CNN — Convolutional Neural Network
Especially useful for images. CNNs can also be used for text tasks by detecting local patterns such as short word sequences.

RNN — Recurrent Neural Network
Processes sequences step by step, carrying information from earlier steps to later ones. Long-range dependencies can be difficult to learn.

LSTM and GRU
Special kinds of recurrent networks designed to manage information over longer sequences more effectively than basic RNNs.

Transformer
Uses attention to model relationships between tokens and can process training sequences in parallel. It forms the foundation of many modern LLMs.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why did Transformers become so important?

RNNs process tokens sequentially, which makes parallelizing sequence computation harder. They can also struggle to preserve information across very long sequences.
LSTMs and GRUs address some of these difficulties, but still retain sequential processing.
Transformers use self-attention to let each token incorporate information from other relevant tokens. This supports efficient parallel training and effective modeling of long-range relationships,
although attention cost and context length still have practical limits.
